use std
into mix.amni

Imports: os, json, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion, gfx.scene3d and spring (the local module spring.amni; its `mquat`, `pos` and `qconj` are used unqualified). This file is a module with no main. It plays the companion's humanoid animation clips on an avatar: clips are retargeted on the page into frames of 91 floats at 30 frames per second (22 slot rotations as quaternions x, y, z, w in floats 0..87, then the hips' local position in floats 88..90), and this module samples, crossfades and poses them, applies the page's per-slot overrides, and packs the posed bones back for the page.

Module state: `var item = -1`, `var asset = -1`, `var slot_node = int[22] { -1, … }` (global glTF node of each humanoid slot, -1 when missing; written with a loop), `var rest_q = linalg::Quat[22]` (each the identity at first), `var cur_q = linalg::Quat[22]` (the posed local rotation of each slot), `var hips_t = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }` (posed local position of slot 0), `var frames f32[>..]`, `var clip_first int[>..]`, `var clip_nf int[>..]`, `var clip_loop bool[>..]`, and the actions: `var act_clip int[>..]`, `var act_t f32[>..]`, `var act_w f32[>..]`, `var act_dw f32[>..]` (weight change per second), `var act_done bool[>..]`, plus `var cur = -1` (the current action's index into those lists). Inertialization state (transitions switch clips instantly and decay the pose difference away, as in Gears of War and Unreal): `var pose_q = linalg::Quat[22]` and `var pose_pq = linalg::Quat[22]` (the last two poses `mix_advance` produced, before page overrides), `var pose_h = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }` and `var pose_ph = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }` (the same for the hips position), `var last_dt f32 = 0.0`, per slot `var in_ax = float3[22]`, `var in_x0 = f32[22]`, `var in_v0 = f32[22]`, `var in_t1 = f32[22]`, for the hips `var in_hd = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }`, `var in_hx0 f32 = 0.0`, `var in_hv0 f32 = 0.0`, `var in_ht1 f32 = 0.0`, and `var in_t f32 = 0.0`, `var in_on = false`.  Half-rotation helper joints (see half_joints): `var hh_node int[>..]` (helper node), `var hh_thigh int[>..]` (the joint it follows), `var hh_t float3[>..]` (its local position, the joint's rest position) and `var hh_r linalg::Quat[>..]` (the joint's rest local rotation). Crease helper joints (see crease_bind): `var ch_node int[>..]` (helper node), `var ch_src int[>..]` (the hinge joint whose bend drives it), `var ch_t float3[>..]` (its rest local position), `var ch_dir float3[>..]` (the unit direction it slides along, in its parent's frame), `var ch_a float3[>..]` and `var ch_b float3[>..]` (in the frame of the hinge's parent: the direction of the hinge's own bone at rest and the direction the hinge folds toward, perpendicular to it), `var ch_r linalg::Quat[>..]` (the hinge's rest local rotation), `var ch_rad f32[>..]` (the limb's radius on the folding side) and `var ch_cap f32[>..]` (the furthest it may slide).

`inert_x(x0 f32, v0 f32, t1 f32, t f32) f32` is the offset left at time t of a quintic decay from x0 with velocity v0 that reaches zero position, velocity and acceleration at t1 (Bollo 2018): 0 when `t1 <= 0`, `t >= t1` or `x0 <= 1e-6`; else `a0 = max(0, (-8 v0 t1 - 20 x0) / t1²)`, `A = -(a0 t1² + 6 v0 t1 + 12 x0) / (2 t1⁵)`, `B = (3 a0 t1² + 16 v0 t1 + 30 x0) / (2 t1⁴)`, `C = -(3 a0 t1² + 12 v0 t1 + 20 x0) / (2 t1³)`, and the result `A t⁵ + B t⁴ + C t³ + a0 t² / 2 + v0 t + x0`.

`inert_fit(x0 f32, xp f32, t1 f32, k int)` stores one decay in slot k (k = 22 means the hips): `v0 = if last_dt > 0 { (x0 - xp) / last_dt } else { 0 }`, then `v0 = min(v0, 0)` (an offset moving away is not extrapolated), `t = t1` and, when `v0 < 0`, `t = min(t1, -5 x0 / v0)` so the curve never overshoots; write x0, v0 and t into `in_x0[k]`, `in_v0[k]`, `in_t1[k]`, or into `in_hx0`, `in_hv0`, `in_ht1` when k is 22.

`mix_open(a int, it int, slots i32[:])` sets `asset = a`, `item = it`; for k below 22, `q = slots[k] as int`; when `q >= 0 && q < gltf::assets[a].nodes.count`, `slot_node[k] = gltf::assets[a].nodes.first + q`, `rest_q[k] = gltf::nodes[slot_node[k]].r`, else `slot_node[k] = -1` and `rest_q[k]` the identity; `cur_q[k] = rest_q[k]`, `pose_q[k] = rest_q[k]`, `pose_pq[k] = rest_q[k]`, `in_x0[k] = 0`. `hips_t` is `gltf::nodes[slot_node[0]].t` when slot 0 exists, and `pose_h`, `pose_ph` take the same value. `last_dt = 0`, `in_on = false`. Clear the clips and actions (`cur = -1`). Also clear the six per-target PSD lists and set every `psd_n[k]` to 0.

`mix_clip(nf int, loop bool, src f32[:]) int` appends a clip: `clip_first` gets `frames.len`, `clip_nf` gets nf, `clip_loop` gets loop, and the first `nf * 91` floats of src are appended to `frames`. Returns the clip's index.

`dur(c int) f32` is `(clip_nf[c] - 1) as f32 / 30.0`.

`mix_play(c int, fade f32) bool`: return false when c is out of range. When `cur >= 0 && act_clip[cur] == c && !act_done[cur]`, return true (already playing). Every existing action fades out: `act_dw[i] = -act_w[i] / max(fade, 0.0001)`. If an action of clip c exists, reuse it (set `act_t` 0, `act_w` 0, `act_done` false), else append one (clip c, t 0, w 0, dw 0, done false). Set its weight to 1 and every other action's weight and `act_dw` to 0 (the switch is instant). When `fade <= 0.0001` set `in_on = false` (a hard cut). Otherwise inertialize over `fade` seconds: for each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0`, `s = sample(c, 0.0, k)`, `o = linalg::qmul(pose_q[k], qconj(s))` negated when `o.w < 0`, `l = length of (o.x, o.y, o.z)`; when `l < 1e-7` set `in_x0[k] = 0`; else `in_ax[k] = float3 { o.x, o.y, o.z } / l`, `x0 = 2 atan2(l, o.w)`, `op = linalg::qmul(pose_pq[k], qconj(s))` negated when `op.w < 0`, `xp = 2 atan2(dot of (op.x, op.y, op.z) with in_ax[k], op.w)`, and `inert_fit(x0, xp, fade, k)`. For the hips when slot 0 exists: `d = pose_h - sample_hips(c, 0.0)`, `l = linalg::length3(d)`; when `l < 1e-6`, `in_hx0 = 0`; else `in_hd = d / l` and `inert_fit(l, linalg::dot3(pose_ph - sample_hips(c, 0.0), in_hd), fade, 22)`. Then `in_t = 0`, `in_on = true`. Set `cur` to its index. Return true.

`sample(c int, t f32, k int) linalg::Quat` reads slot k's rotation at time t: `x = clamp(t * 30.0, 0.0, (clip_nf[c] - 1) as f32)`, `i0 = floor(x) as int`, `i1 = min(i0 + 1, clip_nf[c] - 1)`, `u = x - i0 as f32`; with `o0 = clip_first[c] + i0 * 91 + k * 4` and `o1` likewise for i1, return `linalg::qslerp(Quat at o0, Quat at o1, u)` (each built as `linalg::Quat { frames[o], frames[o + 1], frames[o + 2], frames[o + 3] }`). `sample_hips(c int, t f32) float3` is the same frame lookup on floats 88..90, mixed with `linalg::mix3`.

`mix_advance(dt f32) int` steps the actions and poses the avatar (first `last_dt = dt`, and `in_t += dt` when `in_on`); it returns the clip index of the current action when it has just finished (a non-looping clip reaching its end for the first time), else -1. For each action i: `act_t[i] += dt`; with `d = dur(act_clip[i])`: when the clip loops and `d > 0`, wrap `act_t[i]` into [0, d) (subtract d while it is at least d); when it does not loop and `act_t[i] >= d`, clamp it to d and, when `!act_done[i]`, set `act_done[i] = true` and, when `i == cur`, remember `act_clip[i]` as the result. `act_w[i] = clamp(act_w[i] + act_dw[i] * dt, 0.0, 1.0)`; stop the weight change (`act_dw[i] = 0`) once it reaches 0 or 1. Then remove every action other than cur whose weight is 0 and whose dw is not positive (compact the five lists in order, fixing `cur` to its new index). Blend each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0`: `cum = 0`, `q = rest_q[k]`; for each action i with `act_w[i] > 0`: `cum += act_w[i]`, `s = sample(act_clip[i], act_t[i], k)`, `q = if cum == act_w[i] { s } else { linalg::qslerp(q, s, act_w[i] / cum) }`; when `cum < 1` and cum > 0, `q = linalg::qslerp(rest_q[k], q, cum)`; `cur_q[k] = q`. Blend the hips position the same way from `gltf::nodes[slot_node[0]].t` with `sample_hips` and `linalg::mix3` into `hips_t`. When `in_on`: for each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0`, `x = inert_x(in_x0[k], in_v0[k], in_t1[k], in_t)` and, when `x > 0`, `cur_q[k] = linalg::qmul(linalg::qaxis(in_ax[k], x), cur_q[k])`; `hips_t = hips_t + in_hd * inert_x(in_hx0, in_hv0, in_ht1, in_t)` when slot 0 exists; set `in_on = false` once `in_t` is at least every `in_t1[k]` and `in_ht1`. Then shift the history: `pose_pq[k] = pose_q[k]`, `pose_q[k] = cur_q[k]` for every slot, `pose_ph = pose_h`, `pose_h = hips_t`. Then `push()` and return the result.

`push()` writes the pose to the renderer: for each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0`, `n = gltf::nodes[slot_node[k]]`, call `s3d::set_node(item, slot_node[k], if k == 0 { hips_t } else { n.t }, cur_q[k], n.s)`. Then call `half_drive(item)` and `mix_drive()`.

`mix_apply(ov f32[:])` blends the page's overrides into the pose: for each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0` and `w = ov[k * 5 + 4] > 0`, `cur_q[k] = linalg::qslerp(cur_q[k], linalg::Quat { ov[k * 5], ov[k * 5 + 1], ov[k * 5 + 2], ov[k * 5 + 3] }, min(w, 1.0))`; then `push()`.

`mix_rest()` sets every slot's `cur_q`, `pose_q` and `pose_pq` back to `rest_q` and `hips_t`, `pose_h` and `pose_ph` to the hips node's rest translation (when slot 0 exists), `in_on = false`, then `push()`.

`mix_live(out f32[:])` poses the item with `s3d::pose(item)` and packs 12 floats per slot k into out at `12 * k`: when `slot_node[k] < 0`, only `out[12 * k + 11] = 0`; else the world rotation `mquat(motion::world[node])` (x, y, z, w), the world position `pos(motion::world[node])` (3 floats), the parent's world rotation `mquat(motion::world[gltf::nodes[node].parent])` (identity when there is no parent) and 1 in float 11. Then floats 264..266 are the world position of slot 5 (the head) when it exists.

Pose-space correctives (PSD): morph targets on the avatar's meshes that fade in as a joint's bone swings toward a sampled direction, read by a Gaussian radial basis interpolator that is exact at every sample and 0 at rest. `let PSD_SIGMA = 0.5` (radians) and `let PSD_CHILD int[22] = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, -1, 7, 8, 9, -1, 11, 12, 13, -1, 15, 16, 17, -1, 19, 20, 21, -1]` (the slot each slot's bone points at). Per target, growable lists: `var psd_node int[>..]` (global node of a mesh node of the avatar), `var psd_k int[>..]` (morph target index in that mesh), `var psd_slot int[>..]`, `var psd_td float3[>..]` (its sample direction in the slot's basis), `var psd_ui int[>..]` (index of that direction among its slot's samples) and `var psd_w f32[>..]` (current weight). Per slot, fixed arrays of 22: `var psd_n int[22] = [0; 22]` (sample count including the rest direction, 0 when the slot drives nothing), `var psd_off int[22] = [0; 22]` (first sample in psd_ud and psd_gw), `var psd_coff int[22] = [0; 22]` (first coefficient in psd_cm), `var psd_D`, `var psd_F`, `var psd_O` and `var psd_a`, each `float3[22] = [float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }; 22]` (the slot's rest basis in world space: along the bone, forward and outward; psd_a is the bone direction in the slot node's own frame), and `var psd_pq linalg::Quat[22] = [linalg::quat_identity(); 22]` (the rest world rotation of the slot node's glTF parent). Growable `var psd_ud float3[>..]` (sample directions in basis coordinates; each slot's first is the rest direction float3 { 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }), `var psd_cm f32[>..]` (each slot's n by n inverse kernel matrix, row-major) and `var psd_gw f32[>..]` (current weight of each sample).

`psd_dir(flex f32, abd f32) float3` takes degrees: with f and b in radians it returns `float3 { cos(f) * cos(b), sin(f) * cos(b), sin(b) }` (as f32).

`psd_basis()` computes every slot's rest basis. Call `motion::rest(asset)` and `motion::update(asset, gfx::mat4_identity)` so `motion::world` (indexed by global node) holds rest world matrices. The side axis L is `linalg::unit3(pos(motion::world[slot_node[14]]) - pos(motion::world[slot_node[18]]))` when slots 14 and 18 exist, else the same from slots 7 and 11 when they exist, else float3 { 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }. With U = float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 }, the global forward is `Fg = linalg::unit3(linalg::cross3(L, U))`. For each slot k with `slot_node[k] >= 0`, `c = PSD_CHILD[k]`, `c >= 0`, `slot_node[c] >= 0` and the two world positions more than 1.0e-5 apart: `D = linalg::unit3(pos(motion::world[slot_node[c]]) - pos(motion::world[slot_node[k]]))`; `psd_a[k] = linalg::qrotate(qconj(mquat(motion::world[slot_node[k]])), D)`; with `pn = gltf::nodes[slot_node[k]].parent`, `psd_pq[k]` is `mquat(motion::world[pn])` when pn >= 0, else the identity; `F = Fg - D * linalg::dot3(D, Fg)`, replaced by `U - D * linalg::dot3(D, U)` when its length is below 0.2, then `linalg::unit3`; `O = linalg::unit3(linalg::cross3(D, F))`; the side s is 1 for slots 6..9 and 14..17, -1 for slots 10..13 and 18..21, else 0, and when s != 0 and `linalg::dot3(O, L) * s < 0` negate O. Store D, F and O in psd_D, psd_F and psd_O.

`mix_psd_add(node int, k int, slot int, dir float3)` appends node, k, slot and dir to psd_node, psd_k, psd_slot and psd_td, 0 to psd_ui and 0.0 to psd_w.

`mix_psd_ready()` builds each slot's samples and inverse kernel matrix. Clear psd_ud, psd_cm and psd_gw. For each slot k below 22 set `psd_n[k] = 0`; when some target has `psd_slot[t] == k`: `psd_off[k] = psd_ud.len`, push float3 { 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }; for each target t with `psd_slot[t] == k` (in order) find the index j from psd_off[k] on with `linalg::dot3(psd_ud[j], psd_td[t]) > 0.9999`, pushing psd_td[t] and taking its index when there is none, and set `psd_ui[t] = j - psd_off[k]`. Let n be `psd_ud.len - psd_off[k]`. Fill a real n by 2n matrix with A[i][j] = `exp(-(th * th) / (PSD_SIGMA * PSD_SIGMA))`, where th is `acos(clamp(dot3, -1.0, 1.0))` of samples i and j, and the identity on the right; invert by Gauss-Jordan elimination with partial pivoting. When a pivot's absolute value is below 1.0e-12, shrink psd_ud back to psd_off[k] entries and leave psd_n[k] at 0. Otherwise `psd_n[k] = n`, `psd_coff[k] = psd_cm.len`, append the inverse row-major as f32 to psd_cm and n zeros to psd_gw.

`mix_psd_dir(k int) float3` is slot k's current bone direction in its basis coordinates: `v = linalg::qrotate(psd_pq[k], linalg::qrotate(cur_q[k], psd_a[k]))`, returned as `float3 { linalg::dot3(v, psd_D[k]), linalg::dot3(v, psd_F[k]), linalg::dot3(v, psd_O[k]) }`.

`mix_drive()` sets every corrective's weight from the current pose. For each slot k with `psd_n[k] > 0` and `psd_n[k] <= 32`: `u = mix_psd_dir(k)`, `n = psd_n[k]`, `o = psd_off[k]`; fill a local `real[32]` phi with `exp(-(th * th) / (PSD_SIGMA * PSD_SIGMA))` for b below n, th being `acos(clamp(linalg::dot3(u, psd_ud[o + b]), -1.0, 1.0))`; then for a below n, `psd_gw[o + a]` is the sum over b of `psd_cm[psd_coff[k] + a * n + b] * phi[b]` (as f32). Then for each target t, with `k = psd_slot[t]`: `w` is `clamp(psd_gw[psd_off[k] + psd_ui[t]], 0.0, 1.0)` when `psd_n[k] > 0`, else 0; `psd_w[t] = w`; when `item >= 0` and `psd_node[t] >= 0` call `s3d::set_weight(item, psd_node[t], psd_k[t], w)`.

`mix_swing(k int, dir float3) linalg::Quat` is the local rotation of slot k that points its bone along the basis direction dir from rest: `s = linalg::unit3(psd_D[k] * dir.x + psd_F[k] * dir.y + psd_O[k] * dir.z)`, `c = linalg::dot3(psd_D[k], s)`; return `rest_q[k]` when c > 0.999999; the axis is `linalg::cross3(psd_D[k], s)`, or psd_F[k] when that is shorter than 1.0e-6; `qw = linalg::qaxis(linalg::unit3(axis), acos(clamp(c, -1.0, 1.0)))`; return `linalg::qnorm(linalg::qmul(qconj(psd_pq[k]), linalg::qmul(qw, linalg::qmul(psd_pq[k], rest_q[k]))))`.

`mix_set(k int, q linalg::Quat)` sets `cur_q[k] = q` when k is in 0..22.

`mix_psd_load(path const byte[:]) int` registers the corrective targets named in the avatar file and returns how many. Return 0 when `asset < 0` or the file cannot be read into a byte list with `read_file`. Clear the six per-target lists. The glb's JSON chunk length is the little-endian u32 at byte 12; parse bytes 20 to 20 + length with `json::parse` into a `json::Doc` (return 0 on failure). For each mesh of the root's "meshes" array, at index mi in order, take its "extras" object's "targetNames" array when both exist; for each string in it, at index t, that starts with "psd:": split the rest on ':' into exactly three parts, a joint name and two numbers flex and abd (`parse_flt`; skip the name otherwise); `jn = gltf::find_node(asset, joint)`; skip when negative or when no slot k has `slot_node[k] == jn`; then for every node nd of the asset (global indices `gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first` up to plus `nodes.count`) with `gltf::nodes[nd].mesh == gltf::assets[asset].meshes.first + mi`, call `mix_psd_add(nd, t, k, psd_dir(flex as f32, abd as f32))`. When any target was added, call `psd_basis()` and `mix_psd_ready()`. Return the target count.

`half_joints(asset int, kids int[:], crease f32[:]) int` adds helper joints, the way game rigs keep hip creases, knees and elbows from collapsing in deep flexion. A joint `kids[q]` with `q < crease.len && crease[q] != 0.0` is a crease joint: it gets no half joint and is skipped by everything below until the last step, which gives it crease helpers. Every other joint gets a half-rotation helper: for each such joint node in kids (global indices) a helper sits at the joint's pivot as a child of the joint's parent and turns half as far as the joint, and skin weights shared by that parent and the joint are spread over parent, helper and joint so no linear blend spans more than half the bend. Return 0 without changes when `asset < 0`, when `hh_node.len > 0 || ch_node.len > 0`, or when the asset's nodes are not the last ones (`gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first + gltf::assets[asset].nodes.count != gltf::nodes.len`). For each index q below kids.len with `th = kids[q]`: skip when it is a crease joint, when th < 0, when `gltf::nodes[th].has_matrix` or when `p = gltf::nodes[th].parent` is negative; let `h = gltf::nodes.len` and push `gltf::Node { parent: p, mesh: -1, skin: -1, children: gltf::Span { first: 0, count: 0 }, t: gltf::nodes[th].t, r: linalg::quat_identity(), s: float3 { 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 }, matrix: gfx::mat4_identity, has_matrix: false, weights: gltf::Span { first: 0, count: 0 }, name: gltf::keep_name(nm[..]) }`, where nm is a local byte list holding `gltf::text_of(gltf::nodes[th].name)` followed by "_half", onto gltf::nodes (name these fields only; the struct may have more with defaults); add 1 to `gltf::assets[asset].nodes.count`; with `ch = gltf::nodes[p].children` and `at = gltf::ints.len`, push `gltf::ints[ch.first + k]` for k in ch.count and then h onto gltf::ints, and set `gltf::nodes[p].children = gltf::Span { first: at, count: ch.count + 1 }`; push h, th, `gltf::nodes[th].t` and `gltf::nodes[th].r` onto hh_node, hh_thigh, hh_t and hh_r. When hh_node is still empty skip the skin and weight work that follows. Otherwise, for each skin sk from `gltf::assets[asset].skins.first` (count `gltf::assets[asset].skins.count`), with `js = gltf::skins[sk].joints` and `ib = gltf::skins[sk].inverse_binds`, use local growable arrays pj, tj and hj with one entry per helper, each -1 at first: for each helper i, pj[i] and tj[i] are the first positions k below js.count where `gltf::ints[js.first + k]` equals `gltf::nodes[hh_node[i]].parent` and `hh_thigh[i]`. Skip the skin when no helper has both pj[i] and tj[i] >= 0. Otherwise, with `at = gltf::ints.len` and `am = gltf::matrices.len`, push the js.count joints `gltf::ints[js.first + k]` onto gltf::ints and the js.count matrices `gltf::matrices[ib.first + k]` onto gltf::matrices; then for each helper i with both pj[i] and tj[i] >= 0 set `hj[i] = gltf::ints.len - at`, push hh_node[i] onto gltf::ints and push `gfx::mul(linalg::compose(float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 } - hh_t[i], linalg::quat_identity(), float3 { 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 }), gltf::matrices[ib.first + pj[i]])` onto gltf::matrices (the helper's rest skinning matrix equals its parent's, so the bind shape is unchanged); set `gltf::skins[sk].joints = gltf::Span { first: at, count: gltf::ints.len - at }` and `gltf::skins[sk].inverse_binds = gltf::Span { first: am, count: gltf::matrices.len - am }`. Then spread the weights, keeping a local `var done int[>..] = []` of mesh indices: for each node nd from `gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first` (count `nodes.count`) with `gltf::nodes[nd].skin == sk`, let `m = gltf::nodes[nd].mesh`; skip when m < 0 or m is already in done, else push it. For each primitive pi from `gltf::meshes[m].prims.first` (count `prims.count`) with `gltf::prims[pi].skinned`, for each vertex v below `gltf::prims[pi].vcount` with `b = (gltf::prims[pi].vfirst + v) * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`: influence c (c in 4) has joint `gltf::verts[b + 18 + c] as int` and weight `gltf::verts[b + 22 + c]`. For each helper i with hj[i] >= 0 find ip, the first influence with joint pj[i] and weight > 0, and it, the first with joint tj[i] and weight > 0; keep the helper (and its ip and it) when both exist, choosing the one whose joint weight (the weight at it) is largest when several helpers qualify; skip the vertex when none does. With `sw = weight(ip) + weight(it)` and `w = weight(it) / sw`: when w <= 0.5 set weight(ip) = sw·(1 − 2w), joint(it) = hj[i] as f32 and weight(it) = sw·2w; otherwise set joint(ip) = hj[i] as f32, weight(ip) = sw·(2 − 2w) and weight(it) = sw·(2w − 1). Last step: for each index q below kids.len that is a crease joint, in order, call `crease_bind(asset, kids[q], crease[q])`. Return `hh_node.len + ch_node.len`.

`half_drive(it int)` turns each helper half as far as its joint has turned from rest. Return when it < 0. For each helper index i: `var l = hh_r[i]`; for each o in `s3d::node_ov` with `o.item == it && o.node == hh_thigh[i]` set `l = o.r`; `var d = linalg::qmul(l, qconj(hh_r[i]))`, negated in all four components when `d.w < 0.0`; call `s3d::set_node(it, hh_node[i], hh_t[i], linalg::qnorm(linalg::Quat { d.x, d.y, d.z, d.w + 1.0 }), float3 { 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 })` (normalizing the quaternion plus the identity halves its angle). Then each crease helper slides: for each index i below ch_node.len: `var l = ch_r[i]`, replaced by `o.r` for the o in `s3d::node_ov` with `o.item == it && o.node == ch_src[i]`; `let d = linalg::qmul(l, qconj(ch_r[i]))`; `let v = linalg::qrotate(d, ch_a[i])` (where the hinge's bone points now); `let c = linalg::dot3(v, ch_a[i])` and `let sn = linalg::dot3(v, ch_b[i])`; the tangent of half the bend toward the folding side is `tn = if sn <= 0.0 { 0.0 } else { sn / max(linalg::length3(float3 { sn, c, 0.0 }) + c, 0.0001) }`; `y = min(ch_rad[i] * tn, ch_cap[i])`; call `s3d::set_node(it, ch_node[i], ch_t[i] + ch_dir[i] * y, linalg::quat_identity(), float3 { 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 })`.

`crease_bind(asset int, th int, kd f32)` gives the hinge joint node th (a knee or an elbow) two crease helper joints, the way film and game rigs keep the inside of a deep bend from folding through itself. On the folding side the two limb surfaces meet on the plane that halves the bend, at distance rad·tan(θ/2) from the joint along either bone (rad = the limb's radius on that side, θ = the bend), so the skin there has to slide that far away from the joint: up the parent's bone and down the joint's own. One helper rides the parent and slides up it, the other rides the joint and slides down it (half_drive moves them), and a vertex hands each helper the share g of the weight it had on that bone, with g falling from 1 on the fold line at the joint to 0 at the limb's sides and at distance D along the bone. The slide runs along the surface. Only meshes that cover the fold line itself take part: a garment that starts past it (a knee sock whose cuff sits below the knee pit) keeps its own weights, so its stripes stay level while the skin slides along underneath it, and garments that do cover the fold (trousers, sleeves) slide with the skin and stay stacked. The outside of the bend (kneecap, elbow tip) keeps the model's own weights. The sign of kd says which way the hinge folds: positive when the joint's bone swings toward +z (elbows; avatars face +z), negative toward −z (knees). `abs(kd)` is D in radii. Return without changes when `th < 0`, when `gltf::nodes[th].has_matrix`, when `p = gltf::nodes[th].parent` is negative or when the asset's nodes are not the last ones (the test half_joints uses). Measure in the first skin sk of the asset (skins from `gltf::assets[asset].skins.first`, count `gltf::assets[asset].skins.count`) whose joint list (`js = gltf::skins[sk].joints`; joint k is node `gltf::ints[js.first + k]`) holds p (at position pj), th (at tj) and a child of th (at cj): the child is the first c among `gltf::ints[gltf::nodes[th].children.first + q]`, q below `gltf::nodes[th].children.count`, that the list holds; keep it as gc. Return when no skin qualifies. With `ib = gltf::skins[sk].inverse_binds`: `o = pos(linalg::inverse(gltf::matrices[ib.first + tj]))` (spring's `pos`, the translation of a matrix), pp the same for pj and ce for cj; `qp = mquat(linalg::inverse(gltf::matrices[ib.first + pj]))` (spring's `mquat`, the parent's bind rotation); `u2 = linalg::unit3(ce - o)`; the limb axis `a = linalg::unit3(linalg::unit3(o - pp) + u2)`; `fz = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, if kd > 0.0 { 1.0 } else { -1.0 } }`; the fold direction `fb = linalg::unit3(fz - a * linalg::dot3(fz, a))`. Vertex terms, for a vertex at float offset b (as in half_joints) of a mesh drawn with a skin in whose joint list p and th sit at positions jp and jt: bind position `v = float3 { gltf::verts[b + gltf::AT_POS], gltf::verts[b + gltf::AT_POS + 1], gltf::verts[b + gltf::AT_POS + 2] }`, `t = linalg::dot3(v - o, a)`, `rv = v - o - a * t`, `rho = linalg::length3(rv)`, `x = linalg::dot3(rv, fb)` (how far toward the folding side), ip = the first influence c (c in 4) with joint `gltf::verts[b + 18 + c] as int == jp` and weight `gltf::verts[b + 22 + c] > 0.0` (-1 when none), ic the same for jt, wp and wc their weights (0.0 when missing), `s = wp + wc` and tot = the sum of the four weights. Walking the meshes means: for each skin s2 of the asset whose joint list holds both p and th (jp and jt their positions in it), each node of the asset with `skin == s2` and a mesh, each mesh once per skin (a local done list), each primitive with `skinned`, each vertex. Walk 1: over the vertices with `wp > 0.2 * s && wc > 0.2 * s` (the model's own transition ring), rad = the largest x and R = the largest rho. Return when no vertex qualifies or `rad <= 0.0`. `D = abs(kd) * rad`. Then add two nodes the way half_joints adds one (push a gltf::Node with the same fields, add 1 to the asset's node count, re-push the parent's children with the new node appended): hp with parent p, `t: gltf::nodes[th].t` and the name `gltf::text_of(gltf::nodes[p].name)` followed by "_crease"; then hc with parent th, `t: float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }` and th's name followed by "_crease". Push onto the ch_ lists, hp's entry first and hc's second: ch_node hp, hc; ch_src th, th; ch_t `gltf::nodes[th].t`, `float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }`; ch_dir `float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 } - linalg::unit3(gltf::nodes[th].t)` (toward the parent's own pivot), `linalg::unit3(gltf::nodes[gc].t)`; and the same values for both: ch_a `aa = linalg::qrotate(gltf::nodes[th].r, linalg::unit3(gltf::nodes[gc].t))`, ch_b `linalg::unit3(bb - aa * linalg::dot3(bb, aa))` with `bb = linalg::qrotate(qconj(qp), fb)`, ch_r `gltf::nodes[th].r`, ch_rad rad and ch_cap `0.9 * D`. Walk 2, per skin s2, before its meshes: with its `js`, `ib`, `at = gltf::ints.len` and `am = gltf::matrices.len`, push its js.count joints and inverse binds onto gltf::ints and gltf::matrices again (as half_joints does), then `hjp = gltf::ints.len - at`, push hp and the matrix `gfx::mul(linalg::compose(float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 } - gltf::nodes[th].t, linalg::quat_identity(), float3 { 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 }), gltf::matrices[ib.first + jp])`, then `hjc = gltf::ints.len - at`, push hc and a copy of `gltf::matrices[ib.first + jt]` (at rest both helpers skin exactly like the bones they ride, so the bind shape is unchanged), and set the skin's joints and inverse_binds spans to the new runs. Then, per mesh of that skin: skip the mesh unless one of its vertices has `s > 0.0 && s >= 0.5 * tot`, `x > 0.5 * rad`, `abs(t) < 0.5 * rad` and `rho <= 1.6 * R` (a mesh without one does not cover the fold line); for each of its vertices with `s > 0.0 && s >= 0.5 * tot`, `x > 0.0` and `rho <= 1.6 * R`: `g = clamp(x / rad, 0.0, 1.0) * max(0.0, 1.0 - abs(t) / D)`; skip when `g <= 0.0`. When ip >= 0 and some influence e has weight 0.0 (the first such): set joint(e) = `hjp as f32`, weight(e) = `wp * g` and weight(ip) = `wp * (1.0 - g)`. Then when ic >= 0 and some influence e still has weight 0.0 (the first such, after the write above): set joint(e) = `hjc as f32`, weight(e) = `wc * g` and weight(ic) = `wc * (1.0 - g)`.
